      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:6:6:78:5",
      "text": [
        " إِنَّا لَنَبْدَأُ بِالْخَلِّ عِنْدَنَا كَمَا تَبْدَءُونَ بِالْمِلْحِ عِنْدَكُمْ فَإِنَّ الْخَلَّ لَيَشُدُّ الْعَقْلَ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Muhammad, from Ahmad Bin Abu Abdullah, from Aban Bin Abdul Malik, from Ismail Bin Jabir, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> having said: We<sup>asws</sup> begin with the vinegar in our<sup>asws</sup> presence, just as you all are beginning with the salt in your presence, for the vinegar strengthens the intellect’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "5. Ali ibn Muhammad has narrated from Ahmad ibn abu ‘Abd Allah from Aban ibn ‘Abd al-Malik from ’Isma‘il ibn Jabir who has said the following: “Abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ‘We begin with vinegar which is with us as you begin with salt which is with you, and vinegar strengthens the ability to understand better.’” "
        ]
      }
